Compile the bit conversions of Float and Double as inline code.

Float.floatToIntBits, Float.intBitsToFloat, Double.doubleToLongBits and
Double.longBitsToDouble are natives, so each call from compiled code goes
through the full VM transition. Recognize them by class, method name and
return type when compiling an invokestatic and emit the conversion directly.
The conversions to bits keep the natives' result, the canonical NaN (0x7fc00000
and 0x7ff8000000000000) for every NaN, with a compare and two conditional
moves; the conversions from bits are a single register transfer to the VFP
register. Constant operands are folded at compile time. Only VFP builds use
this; other builds keep calling the natives.

